001100 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
001200 PROGRAM-ID.          SFREIGHT.
001300 AUTHOR.              L BUNN / B WINTER.
001400 DATE-WRITTEN.        JUNE 6, 1983.
001500 DATE-COMPILED.
001600*INSTALLATION.        GOODYEAR TIRE AND RUBBER - AKRON.
001700*SECURITY.
001800*REMARKS.
001900*           REWRITTEN DECEMBER 1984 BY BARBARA WINTER.
002000*           COMBINED AKRON'S PROGRAM WITH SUBPLANT'S PROGRAM.
002100*************************************************************
002200*************************************************************
002300**                    S F R E I G H T                      **
002400*D      THIS SUBROUTINE PROCESSES THE FREIGHT INFORMATION  **
002500*D    FOR A RECEIVING SLIP.  IF THE FREIGHT HAS BEEN       **
002600*D    ENTERED ALREADY FROM ANOTHER PURCHASE ORDER, THEN    **
002700*D    THAT FREIGHT DATA IS COPIED INTO A NEW FREIGHT       **
002800*D    SEGMENT FOR THE NEW RECEIVING SLIP.  OTHERWISE,      **
002900*D    THE USER MUST ENTER FREIGHT DATA IN THIS SUBROUTINE. **
003000**                                                         **
003100**    DATABASE UPDATES:                                    **
003200**     DDAILYTC   PUT      350 TC PER P.O. (FREIGHT)       **
003300**                PUT      352 TC PER P.O. (FREIGHT)       **
003400**     DPOFREIGHT PUT      ENTIRE RECORD FOR THIS R.S.     **
003500**                PUT      ONLY REFERBACK FOR MULTI-P.O.S  **
003600**     MPORCV     PUT      NEW RS ENTRY ('  ' STATUS)      **
003700**                UPDATE   ACCUMULATOR (RS # IN STATUS).   **
003800**     MPLTINFO   UPDATE   ADD 1 TO SEQUENCE NUMBER.       **
003900*************************************************************
004000*                      PROGRAM CHANGES                      *
004100*************************************************************
004200*    JANUARY 30, 1985                          B. WINTER
004300*         ZBILL FOR AKRON WAS NOT BEING STORED IN
004400*         DPOFREIGHT UNTIL NOW.
004500*    FEBRUARY 15, 1985                         B. WINTER
004600*         ADDED "U" FOR UPS AND "D" FOR LOCAL PICKUP
004700*         TO FREIGHT TYPE.
004800*    MARCH 12, 1985                            B. WINTER
004900*         THE INVOICE SYSTEM NOW PUTS OUT A FREIGHT SEGMENT,
005000*         SO A CHECK WAS ADDED IN THE MULTI-FREIGHT LOGIC.
005100*         IF A REFER-BACK PO IS SPACES, IT WILL NOT BE
005200*         CONSIDERED A MULTI-FREIGHT PO FOR RECEIVING.
005300*    APRIL 18, 1985                            B. WINTER
005400*         ADDED FREIGHT DATE CHECK:  DATE CANNOT BE A FUTURE
005500*         DATE AND CANNOT BE OLDER THAN BEFORE LAST YEAR.
005600*    JULY 29, 1985                             B. WINTER
005700*         GENERAL CHANGES:
005800*           SEQUENCE NUMBER IN MPORCV RECEIVER ENTRY IS
005900*           INCREMENTED FOR ALL PLANTS EVEN THOUGH KELLY
006000*           PLANTS ONLY USE IT.
006100*         KELLY CHANGES:
006200*           1.  CARRIER ID IS REQUIRED ON FREIGHT SCREEN.
006300*           2.  EITHER CARRIER'S WEIGHT OR OUR WEIGHT MUST
006400*               BE ENTERED FOR RAW MATERIALS.
006500*    OCTOBER 30, 1985
006600*      1. CHANGED PROGRAM TO BE COMPATIBLE WITH THE NATIVE
006700*         LANGUAGE SUPPORT FACILITY.      PAUL D RAGLOW.
006800*    NOVEMBER, 1985                BARBARA WINTER
006900*         ADDED CHECK TO ENTER PACKING SLIP FOR "PAY UPON RECEIPT"
007000*         VENDORS.
007100*    MAY 7, 1986                   BARBARA WINTER
007200*     CHANGED THE LOGIC FOR MULTI PO'S.  NOW THE ORIGINAL
007300*     PO IS THE ONLY ONE THAT CONTAINS ALL INFORMATION IN
007400*     DPOFREIGHT SEGMENT.  THE SUCESSIVE PO'S WILL ONLY
007500*     CONTAIN THE REFERBACK PO IN BOTH THE REFERBACK FIELD
007600*     AND THE FREIGHT BILL NUMBER, AND THE RECEIVED DATE.
007700*   JUNE 24, 1986                 BARBARA WINTER.
007800*      THE FREIGHT CHARGES ON THE SCREEN WAS X(8) AND THE
007900*      TRANSACTION FIELD WAS 9(7), SO THE RIGHT BIT WAS BEING
008000*      DROPPED.  ADDED A REDEFINING CLAUSE TO THE SCREEN FIELD
008100*      OF 9(8) WHICH SOLVED THE PROBLEM OF CHARGES BEING RIGHT
008200*      SHIFTED BY ONE DIGIT.
      *C  NOVEMBER 2, 1992              JEFF BUNGO
      *C     ADDED CODE TO CHECK WEIGHT OF RAW MATERIAL RECEIVED
      *C     AGAINST THE CARRIER'S WEIGHT ENTERED ON THE FREIGHT
      *C     SCREEN.  THIS CHECK IS ONLY DONE FOR INVOICELESS PO'S
      *C     AND THE NET WEIGHT RECEIVED FOR THE PO IS CALCULATED
      *C     FOR RAW MATERIAL ITEMS IN POUNDS ONLY.  THE RAW MATERIAL
      *C     GROUPS WERE NEEDED TO BE PASSED FROM SRCVEXEC, AS WELL AS
      *C     THE ITEM LINES.  IF THE RECEIVED WEIGHT EXCEEDS THE AMOUNT
      *C     ENTERED ON THE FREIGHT SCREEN, THEN A NEW SCREEN WILL
      *C     APPEAR LISTING THOSE ITEMS AND THE NET WEIGHT RESULTING.
      *C     THE USER WILL HAVE THE OPTION TO CONTINUE OR TO END THE
      *C     PROCESSING OF THE RECEIVING SLIP.
      *C  JANUARY 12, 1993              JEFF BUNGO, REQ #6344
      *C     IF THERE ARE MORE THAN 12 ITEMS ON THE RECEIVING SLIP
      *C     A FREIGHT ACCUMULATOR RECORD IS WRITTEN FOR THE PO
      *C     SO THAT WHEN THE "MORE THAN 12" ITEMS ARE PROCESSED
      *C     A FREIGHT REFER BACK WILL BE WRITTEN FOR THAT NEW
      *C     RECEIVING SLIP WITH "MORE THAN 12" BACK TO THE
      *C     FIRST RECEIVING SLIP WITH "12 ITEMS".
      *C     A SPECIAL CHECK MUST BE MADE TO MAKE SURE WE ARE NOT
      *C     REFERING BACK TO REFERBACK.
      *C  MARCH   12, 1993              CATHY KALMAN, REQ #6385
      *C     ADDED LOGIC AND A SCREEN SO USER CAN ENTER MULTIPLE
      *C     PO'S FOR ONE FREIGHT BILL WITH MORE THAN ONE PACKING
      *C     SLIP. THIS SCREEN WILL ONLY SHOW WHEN RECEIVING
      *C     INVOICELESS PO'S.
      *C
      *C  DECEMBER 4, 1996  JEFF BUNGO  REQ 96-035
      *C     PASS CARRIER BACK TO SRCVEXEC FOR QS9000 TRACKING.
      *C
      *C  APRIL 30, 1997     JEFF BUNGO
      *C     ALLOW FOR RECEIPT VERIFICATION OF AN ASN.  THE FREIGHT
      *C     SEGMENT HAS ALREADY BEEN ADDED AND THE RS NUMBER IS PASSED
      *C     AS A NEW PARAM ASN-RECEIVER.  RETRIEVE THE RECEIVER TO
      *C     DISPLAY ASN VALUES ON THE FRT SCREEN AND REWRITE INSTEAD
      *C     OF WRITING A NEW RECORD FOR THE FREIGHT SEGMENT.
      *C
      *C  JULY 22, 1997      CA YODER
      *C     ADDED EDIT CHECK TO ONLY ALLOW PREPAID FREIGHT FOR
      *C     GOODYEAR-TO-GOODYEAR SHIPMENTS ("IT" ORDERS).  DANVILLE
      *C     REPORTED A PROBLEM WITH "IT"S BEING MARKED AS COLLECT;
      *C     GARY STARCHER SAID THAT THEY ARE ONLY SHIPPED OUT AS
      *C     PREPAID.
      *C
      *C  OCTOBER 30, 1997   CA YODER
      *C     ADDED CENTURY FOR DATABASE CHANGE TO MCFPCSTERM.
      *C
      *C  NOVEMBER 11, 1997  JEFF BUNGO
      *C     CHANGED RECEIVING TO USE A SUBFILE TO HOLD ALL ITEMS
      *C     INSTEAD OF LIMITING EACH RECEIVER TO 12 ITEMS AND
      *C     DO FREIGHT REFERBACK TO FIRST RECEIVER FOR SUBSEQUENT
      *C     GROUPS OF 12.  THE SORT TABLE OF ITEMS, RAW MATERIAL
      *C     GROUPS, ANY MORE ITEMS FLAG, AND RCVR FLAG ARE NO LONGER
      *C     PASSED AS PARAMETERS TO THIS PROGRAM FROM SRCVEXEC.
      *C     A NEW PARM NET RAW WEIGHT (CALCULATED IN SRCVEXEC) WILL
      *C     BE PASSED TO CHECK RAW MATERIAL WEIGHT VS. WEIGHT ENTERED
      *C     ON THE FREIGHT SCREEN.  ONLY THE TOTAL WEIGHT OF ITEMS RECIEVED
      *C     CAN NOW BE DISPLAYED INSTEAD OF EACH ITEM.  ALSO ALL REFERENCES
      *C     TO FREIGHT REFERBACK FOR RECEIVERS WITH > 12 ITEMS HAS BEEN
      *C     REMOVED.
      *C
      *C  JULY 28, 1998   CA YODER
      *C     ADDED CALLS TO TDATECK2 TO WRITE OUT THE FREIGHT BILL DATE
      *C     IN THE CORRECT FORMAT TO DPOFREIGHT AND DDAILYTC.
      *C
      *C  MAY 7, 1999     DAVE PLUM
      *C     CORRECTED A PROBLEM WITH RECORDS BEING WRITTEN TO DDAILYTC
      *C     WITH A BAD TRANSACTION DATE AND A BLANK TRANSACTION TIME.
      *C
      *C  OCT 12,2000     JIM COFFMAN
      *C     CHANGED LENGTH OF ALL-PO-RLSE VARIABLE PASSED IN LINKAGE
      *C     SECTION TO AGREE WITH WHAT IS PASSED FROM SRCVEXEC
      *C     (DE-FIELDS-1-PO).
      ******************************************************************
